// Stands in for back/link/ext/decl/size.id's complete_arr, which the parser's
// decl_leaf calls to give `int a[] = {...}` its length. The real one counts the
// initializer through the back end's string-literal decoder, so it cannot be
// built from the front end alone; a parse tree does not depend on it, because
// the declaration node keeps the initializer and the unsized type either way.
complete_arr(int ty, int a) {
  int r = ty;
} return int r;
